Title: RxJava 1.x onCompleted is never called?
Description: Hi, 

I have the following code to demonstrate the problem.

```Java
CountDownLatch latch = new CountDownLatch(1);
        
Observable<Integer> stream1 = Observable.range(1, 3);
Observable<Integer> stream2 = stream1
        .flatMap(a -> {
            return Observable.fromEmitter(emitter -> {
                Thread t = new Thread(() -> {
                    if (a == 3) {
                        emitter.onCompleted();
                    } else {
                        emitter.onNext(a + 1000);
                    }
                });
                System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " Created a-thread for " + a);
                t.setName("a-thread");
                t.start();
            }, Emitter.BackpressureMode.NONE);
        });
        stream2
                .doOnUnsubscribe(()-> System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " Unsubscribed."))
                .subscribe(a -> {
                    System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " processing: " + a);
                },
                System.err::println,
                () -> {
                    System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " processed complete.");
                    latch.countDown();
                });
latch.await();
```

I am expecting " processed complete." will be called but it never did. I am using rxJava 1.2.2.
Also, would the Observer#onCompleted being called if the "emitter.onCompleted()" had been commented out from the above?

